Feature 1: Infinite scroll
“Number one: infinite scroll. A newspaper ends. A TV show ends. A book has a last page. When was the last time you reached the bottom of your feed? [Pause.]
You can’t, because there isn’t one. There’s no natural stopping point, so you have to make the decision to stop yourself, and that takes real effort.”


Feature 2: Autoplay
“Number two: autoplay. Think of the countdown that starts the next episode on a streaming app, or the next video that begins on its own.
Notice what this does. The next video starts before you’ve decided whether you want it. Stopping now requires an action, while carrying on requires none. The default has been quietly reversed in the platform’s favour.”


Feature 3: Push notifications
“Number three: push notifications. Think about the last time you put your phone down. What made you pick it up again? [Pause.]
Often it wasn’t a decision. It was a buzz, a banner or a red badge with a number on it. Notifications are designed to pull you back in, and the words are carefully chosen. Look at this one: ‘Come back and see!’ That is a very deliberate invitation.”


Feature 4: Personalised feeds
“Number four: personalised feeds. The platform learns what catches your eye and then gives you more of it.
Over time the feed feels like it was made just for you. That feels wonderful, and it also makes it very hard to put down.”
 
